HST Office: the document windows of the Tabbed user interface draw their own title bar on Windows (gap list G19).

The OS caption and the ribbon tab row become one top row, 48 logical px high as in the reference suite: a drag
band above the unchanged tab row (quick access toolbar, tabs, feature search) and, at its right end, the window
title then minimize, maximize/restore and close drawn in the Windows 10/11 style (46 px buttons, hover and
pressed states, red close, dimmed when inactive, system colours in high contrast, light on a dark theme).
At 100 % this gives back 18 px (31 px caption + 35 px tab row -> 48 px). Ribbon groups, tab row height and the
banner slot are untouched.

- vcl/win (HstWinTitleBar.cxx, hook in SalFrameWndProc): WM_NCCALCSIZE takes the caption out (a maximized
  window keeps its client inside the monitor and one pixel for an auto-hide taskbar); WM_NCHITTEST keeps every
  OS behaviour native: drag areas answer HTCAPTION (move, double-click maximize, Aero Snap, right-click
  system menu; Alt+Space is unchanged), the buttons HTMINBUTTON/HTMAXBUTTON/HTCLOSE (Windows 11 shows Snap
  Layouts on the maximize button), the top edge HTTOP*. Button presses never reach DefWindowProc; the frame
  tracks hover and press, vcl paints them, WM_SYSCOMMAND runs them. WM_GETTITLEBARINFOEX reports the real
  rectangles for UI Automation. A one-pixel DWM frame extension keeps the shadow. Window states stay in
  system-caption terms, so switching between sessions never moves or grows a window.
- vcl (HstTitleBar*.cxx, ImplBorderWindow): wanted for a top-level work window with the Tabbed notebookbar,
  no shown menu bar, not full screen, and the option off; the switch runs asynchronously. Empty parts of the
  tab row are caption, tabs and controls stay client. The tab row keeps room for the caption area through
  hst::titlebar::RowReserve (NotebookbarTabControlBase::ImplPlaceTabs); the title yields before the search box.
- Tools > Options > HST Office > View > Interface > "Use the operating system's title bar"
  (org.openoffice.Office.Common/Misc/HstSystemTitleBar, default false) switches every window at once; shown
  only on Windows. Linux (gtk3) and macOS keep the system title bar.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0); new files MPL-2.0.
Test: tests/unit/test_custom_titlebar.py; tests/realwin/check-custom-titlebar.ps1 on Windows.
